1 NOTE First wife of Livinus Bundervoet and mother of Segerius Bundervoet (~1615–1669), so a
2 CONT direct ancestor. Her given name is all that survives: the paulderidder tree records her
2 CONT as "Elisabeth NN", with no surname, no dates and no parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT SURNAME NOT KNOWN — and specifically not "Hovelynck". Livinus's record here used to
2 CONT call her Elisabeth Hovelynck; the paulderidder tree, which that claim was attributed
2 CONT to, gives no surname at all. The surname has been removed rather than carried forward,
2 CONT because a name that no reachable source states is exactly the kind of detail that
2 CONT hardens into fact by being repeated. If another tree does give a surname, it can be
2 CONT restored with that tree cited.
2 CONT
2 CONT FRONTIER: an Evergem marriage of Livinus Bundervoet in the 1610s would name her in
2 CONT full, and would also settle which of his two marriages came first.
