1 NOTE Source detail: Family (confirmed maiden name). Oostende candidates: Simonne Florida Vandewalle 1913 & Simonne Augusta 1914 — West-Vlaanderen civil birth acts (Geneanet)
2 CONT
2 CONT RESEARCH NOTE. Vandewalle is one of the most common West-Flemish surnames, so isolating her needs a linking record. Two strong Oostende candidates of the right age: (a) Simonne Florida Vandewalle, b. 6 Jun 1913 Oostende — parents Petrus Franciscus Antonius Vandewalle (1884) & Magdalena Clementia Willaert (1888); grandparents Franciscus Eduardus Vandewalle × Mathildis Vandierendounck and Emilius Willaert (1856) × Maria Lauwereins (1856–1893); (b) Simonne Augusta Vandewalle, b. 1914 Oostende. Neither is yet tied to Gustaaf. Decisive record: the Gustaaf × Simonne marriage (Oostende ~1938–40, or England 1940–43) — it would name her parents — or Roland’s 1943 UK birth (mother’s maiden name).
